  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the intensity of the interference pattern in Young&#39;s double slit experiment can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#981;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, the ratio of the required intensities can be calculated as follows-</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
